# Files exempt from the ASCII-only rule.
#
# Everything else in the tree must be pure ASCII: `-` instead of em/en dashes,
# `->` instead of arrows, and any unicode that has to exist as data written as
# a `\u{...}` escape so the source file itself stays ASCII.
#
# The entries below carry unicode that is the content, not typography. Rewriting
# them would change what a user sees, and escaping it would either be impossible
# (Rust raw strings, markup attributes) or destroy the readability that makes the
# file useful.
#
# One path per line, relative to the repo root. Run the checker with:
#   python3 ascii-sanitize.py . --exclude-file tools/ascii-sanitize.exclude

# Example apps: glyphs are the UI. Sparkline bars, status dots, and icon-button
# captions are what the app draws on screen.
apps/datagrid/main.lmn
apps/datagrid/main.rhai
apps/kanban/main.lmn
apps/kanban/main.rhai
apps/kanban/README.md
apps/sysmon/main.cpp
apps/sysmon/main.lmn
apps/tracker/main.lmn
apps/weather/lumen.toml
apps/weather/main.lmn
apps/widget-garden/main.cdl

# Localization fixture: German message catalog. The text is the test data.
lumen/i18n/examples/hello/de-DE.ftl

# Starter-app templates for `lumenc new`. The markup and script bodies live in
# Rust raw strings, which cannot carry `\u{...}` escapes, and the glyphs are the
# generated app's own UI.
lumenc/src/scaffold.rs
